            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Cleopatra's Reign and Politics</strong><br>\nAs a ruler, Cleopatra was known for her clever political maneuvers and efforts to preserve Egypt's independence despite Rome's growing power. She was a patron of arts and education and worked to elevate the economic status of her country. Her rule is noted for significant cultural and scientific achievements, reflecting her desire to foster a renaissance in Egyptian society.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cleopatra and Mark Antony</strong><br>\nCleopatra's next significant Roman alliance was with Mark Antony in 41 BC. Their relationship was both a strategic political move and a personal romance. They had three children together and envisioned a large eastern empire. Their dream would challenge Rome's authority and lead to future conflicts.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Battle of Actium</strong><br>\nThe relationship between Cleopatra and Mark Antony eventually led to the Battle of Actium in 31 BC, where their forces were defeated by Octavian, the future Emperor Augustus of Rome. This defeat was a crucial blow to their ambitions and to the independence of Egypt.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
