          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Cleopatra's Final Years</strong><br>\nAfter the defeat at Actium, Cleopatra's world started to crumble. Egypt was no longer the major power it once was, and Cleopatra's own position was in jeopardy. In the face of Roman aggression, she attempted to negotiate for her children's future and Egypt's autonomy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cleopatra's Legacy</strong><br>\nCleopatra's death in 30 BC marked the end of the Ptolemaic Kingdom and the beginning of Egypt's period as a Roman province. She was the last active ruler of the Ptolemaic era and left behind a legacy that included her efforts to maintain Egypt's prosperity and independence against Rome's dominance.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cleopatra in Historical Memory</strong><br>\nCleopatra has remained a figure of fascination and controversy throughout history. She has been portrayed as a seductress, a strategist, and a sovereign in equal measure. Her life has been the subject of countless works of art, literature, and film, making her one of the most enduring figures of antiquity.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
